    "biography": {
      "concept": "Unarmed courier who brings paperwork to the Proving Ground's final fight (tutorial)",
      "notes": "When the great-circle fight on the Proving Ground turns, a messenger arrives: unarmed, badly rendered, and carrying paperwork, which reads like a surrender composed at speed by something with no idea how a surrender is composed. It wants to hand the documents over, ask everyone to stop, and get through the next minute in one piece."
    }
  },
  "flags": {
    "bbttcc-onboarding": {
      "spawned": true,
      "kind": "foe",
      "foeClass": "sentient",
      "ownerUserId": "rzJQNVz5H3SHfP2i"
    },
    "fourththing": {
      "kind": "npc"
    },
    "bbttcc-mal-voice": {
      "persona": {
        "notes": "[PERSONA-PACKPASS-2026-10-06] PRIVATE TRUTH — A Messenger, Sent In Haste. Voice: breathless, over-formal, glitching ('badly rendered' by design — the art is low-poly and the courier knows it is); every sentence sounds like a capitulation composed at speed by something with no idea how a formal capitulation is composed. WANTS: for the fight to stop — it carries the offer to end it, and it wants the Stewards to take the surrender and open the parley rather than finish what's in the circle. It hands over its paperwork: two Courtly Secrets — \"We're Screwed\" (an unencrypted panic burst sent to everyone at once, clearly not meant for the Stewards: whatever is on the other end has done the arithmetic and does not like it) and \"Please Totally Don't Murder Us, We Give Up For Reals\" (a formal capitulation, signed. Repeatedly). WHAT IT WON'T SAY: what sent it or what was so frightened of the Proving Ground that it tried to unmake it — that is for the parley to find out. ⚙ OWNER SLOT — never improvise who or what the sender is. PRIVATE TRUTH: it is the opposition's courier in the tutorial final showdown, unarmed (a sentient foe, body 2), one per cohort; Mal 'did not have this on the list'. STAGING: arrives when the great-circle fight visibly turns, on the Proving Ground or in the folded court room ('The Parley'); the GM runs the parley from the Raid Console — PRESENCE, not violence. Striking it is possible and pointless.",
        "topics": "the paperwork, the surrender, the offer, stopping, the parley, the circle, the panic burst, signatures"
      }
    }
  },
